{"data":{"codec":"utf8","content_ref":"inline:The claim that a panel of non-experts outperforms a single expert depends on the Law of Large Numbers reducing idiosyncratic error, as proposed in SRC_001; this is refuted if the variance of cognitive biases is systemic rather than stochastic, meaning the checklist induces a shared bias that scales with the panel size.","id":"9fa89068cf4ec1a3171523801f0fc1c08cd40a5d8064e53082b5b38b26610625","interface":{"commitments":["hv-floor@2a45b7988522","lineage-ref@3a67ea0f1135","relation-form@578e42df713e"],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"194ee9db21a270b7c4abb5b02822a42a4fc70ea2285a42a224cdfa69fea99bc4"},{"role":"dependence","target":"44fb9ebb84c6f7ee86183d5d43e419c1ca2fc3a70ff8864a79d92565b05e9c40"},{"role":"dependence","target":"99a975dba6d890d0ba23563eaa5a56e9b086db503ac319b0c6dc864b3f939b84"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ac94841d55e6aae4dc6090714279f90dad636c270045d00b3f596e356fd9ec1c"},{"role":"dependence","target":"e31f362c20e3d13a9717aca7d808e27a7142743a1b0a80fdb7c63c713ab9acf5"}]},"provenance":{"event_seq":1799,"role":"conjecturer","school":"school-0"},"warrants":[]},"id":"9fa89068cf4ec1a3171523801f0fc1c08cd40a5d8064e53082b5b38b26610625","schema":"artifact"}